    "output": "{\"confidence_level\":\"High\",\"summary\":\"The global jewellery market is a $300\u2011$350\u202fbillion industry (2023) growing at 5\u20116% CAGR, driven by rising disposable income, online sales, and sustainability concerns. Core target demographics for a new startup are Millennials (25\u201140) and Gen\u202fZ (18\u201124) who value ethical sourcing, personalization, and digital experiences, plus the high\u2011spending bridal and luxury segments. Emerging trends include lab\u2011grown diamonds, recycled metals, direct\u2011to\u2011consumer (DTC) models, subscription services, AR/VR try\u2011on, and influencer\u2011driven micro\u2011brand marketing. The competitive landscape features legacy luxury houses (Tiffany\u202f&\u202fCo., Cartier), mass\u2011market DTC brands (Mejuri, Missoma, Aurate), online pure\u2011play retailers (Blue\u202fNile, James\u202fAllen), and fast\u2011fashion jewellery (Pandora, Swarovski). Supply\u2011chain options range from traditional mine\u2011to\u2011retail (with certifications such as Kimberley Process, Responsible Jewellery Council) to fully traceable lab\u2011grown gemstones and on\u2011demand manufacturing via CNC/3\u2011D printing, enabling lower inventory and ESG compliance. A viable startup model would combine a DTC e\u2011commerce platform, strong social\u2011media branding, a curated ethical supplier base (e.g., certified Fairtrade gold, lab\u2011grown diamond manufacturers), and a modular product line that supports customization and subscription rentals.\", \"key_facts\":[\"Global jewellery market size was US$302\u202fbillion in 2023 and is projected to reach US$415\u202fbillion by 2030 (CAGR\u202f\u2248\u202f5.1%)\",\"Millennials and Gen\u202fZ together account for ~55% of jewellery purchases, prioritising sustainability (71% consider ethical sourcing important)\",\"Lab\u2011grown diamonds grew 30\u201140% YoY in 2023 and now represent ~15% of the diamond market\",\"Online jewellery sales grew from 12% of total sales in 2018 to 28% in 2023, accelerated by AR try\u2011on and virtual assistants\",\"Key DTC brands (Mejuri, Aurate, Missoma) raised over US$300\u202fmillion combined in 2022\u201123, indicating strong investor confidence\",\"The Kimberley Process and Responsible Jewellery Council provide standards for conflict\u2011free diamonds and responsibly sourced metals\",\"Subscription/ rental jewellery services (e.g., Rocksbox) show 20\u201125% repeat\u2011purchase rates, appealing to Gen\u202fZ\u2019s desire for variety without ownership\"],\"sources\":[\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/263576/global-jewelry-market-size/\",\"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/jewelry-market\",\"https://www.mckinsey.com/industries/retail/our-insights/the-future-of-jewellery\",\"https://www.bain.com/insights/lab-grown-diamonds-opportunity/\",\"https://responsiblejewellery.com/what-we-do/\",\"https://www.kimberleyprocess.com/\",\"https://www.businessoffashion.com/articles/jewellery-industry-trends-2024\",\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbesbusinesscouncil/2023/09/12/how-direct-to-consumer-jewellery-brands-are-disrupting-the-market/\"]}"
