011level encryption; or HIPAA\u2011certified NoSQL (e.g., MongoDB Atlas with encryption) \u2022 Hosting: AWS HIPAA\u2011eligible services (EC2, RDS, S3 with SSE), Azure Health Data Services, or GCP Cloud Healthcare API \u2022 Security: TLS\u202f1.2+, HSTS, regular vulnerability scanning, OWASP Top\u202f10 mitigations, multi\u2011factor authentication\",\"Non\u2011functional requirements include 99.9\u202f% uptime via cloud redundancy, scalability through container orchestration (Kubernetes or AWS ECS), disaster recovery with encrypted backups, and compliance with WCAG\u202f2.1\u202fAA for accessibility\"],\"sources\":[\"U.S. Department of Health & Human Services, \\\"HIPAA Privacy Rule\\\" and \\\"HIPAA Security Rule\\\" (2023) https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/index.html\",\"National Institute of Standards and Technology, SP 800-53 Rev.5 (2020) https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-53/rev-5/final\",\"Office of the National Coordinator for Health IT, \\\"Health IT Playbook\\\" (2022) https://www.healthit.gov/playbook/\",\"World Wide Web Consortium, \\\"Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1\\\" (2021) https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/\",\"OWASP Foundation, \\\"OWASP Top 10 - 2021\\\" https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/\",\"Amazon Web Services, \\\"HIPAA Eligible Services\\\" (2023) https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/hipaa-compliance/\",\"Microsoft Azure, \\\"Azure for Healthcare and HIPAA\\\" (2023) https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/healthcare-apis/\",\"Google Cloud, \\\"Cloud Healthcare API\\\" (2023) https://cloud.google.com/healthcare-api\"]}"
