    "output": "{\"confidence_level\":\"high\",\"summary\":\"A HIPAA\u2011compliant healthcare website must serve patients, clinicians, and administrators while providing secure patient\u2011portal functions, appointment scheduling, tele\u2011health video, billing, and EHR integration. Core requirements include strict privacy and security controls (encryption at rest and in transit, TLS\u202f1.2+, OAuth\u202f2.0/OpenID\u202fConnect, role\u2011based access control, detailed audit logging, rate limiting, secure HTTP headers), WCAG\u202f2.1\u202fAA accessibility, Business Associate Agreements (BAA) for every third\u2011party service, and a comprehensive testing strategy that covers functional, security, performance, and accessibility validation. The solution should be built on a HIPAA\u2011eligible cloud platform, use a modern responsive front\u2011end, and a back\u2011end capable of audit trails and encryption, with regular penetration testing, vulnerability scanning, and compliance audits to maintain continuous adherence to HIPAA and related standards.\",\"key_facts\":[\"HIPAA Security Rule mandates encryption of PHI at rest and in transit, unique user authentication, automatic log\u2011off, audit controls, and breach\u2011notification procedures (45 CFR \u00a7164.312\u2011a,b)\",\"Primary user groups are patients (access health records, schedule visits, pay bills, engage in telehealth), providers (view charts, document encounters, conduct video visits), and staff (billing, reporting, content management)\",\"Patient portal must include secure registration, multi\u2011factor authentication, encrypted messaging, view/download of lab results, medication lists, and consent management\",\"Appointment scheduling requires real\u2011time calendar integration, automated reminders (email/SMS), cancellation policies, and audit logs of all changes\",\"Telehealth video must use end\u2011to\u2011end encrypted streaming (e.g., WebRTC with DTLS/SRTP), session recording consent, and integration with the patient record\",\"Billing module should support secure payment processing (PCI\u2011DSS compliant), insurance eligibility checks, invoicing, and audit trails for all transactions\",\"EHR integration typically uses HL7\u202fv2/FHIR APIs, must enforce token\u2011based authentication, data mapping, and immutable logging of data exchange\",\"Security standards: \u2022 Encryption at rest \u2013 AES\u2011256 for databases and storage buckets \u2022 TLS\u202f1.2+ with HSTS for all web traffic \u2022 OAuth\u202f2.0 / OpenID\u202fConnect for delegated auth, with short\u2011lived access tokens \u2022 RBAC with least\u2011privilege principle; granular permissions for patient, provider, admin roles \u2022 Immutable audit logging for every access/modification of PHI, retained \u22656\u202fyears \u2022 Rate limiting (e.g., 100 requests/min per IP/user) to mitigate abuse \u2022 Secure headers: CSP, X\u2011Frame\u2011Options, X\u2011Content\u2011Type\u2011Options, Referrer\u2011Policy\",\"WCAG\u202f2.1\u202fAA compliance requires perceivable text alternatives, keyboard\u2011navigable UI, sufficient color contrast, resizable text, and screen\u2011reader compatibility for all public and portal pages\",\"Business Associate Agreements must be executed with cloud providers, video\u2011conferencing services, payment gateways, analytics tools, and any SaaS components that handle PHI\",\"Testing strategy: \u2022 Unit & integration tests for all functional flows \u2022 Automated UI tests covering accessibility (axe\u2011core, pa11y) \u2022 Static code analysis (SonarQube) and OWASP Dependency\u2011Check \u2022 Dynamic application security testing (DAST) and regular penetration tests (quarterly) \u2022 Vulnerability scanning (e.g., Nessus, Qualys) \u2022 HIPAA compliance audits (internal & third\u2011party) \u2022 Load & performance testing for telehealth video scalability \u2022 Disaster\u2011recovery drills and backup restoration verification\"],\"sources\":[\"U.S. Department of Health & Human Services, \\\"HIPAA Privacy Rule\\\" and \\\"HIPAA Security Rule\\\" (2023) https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/index.html\",\"National Institute of Standards and Technology, SP 800-66 Revision 1, \\\"An Introductory Resource Guide for Implementing the HIPAA Security Rule\\\" (2020) https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-66/rev-1/final\",\"National Institute of Standards and Technology, SP 800-53 Rev.5 (2020) https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-53/rev-5/final\",\"Office of the National Coordinator for Health IT, \\\"Health IT Playbook\\\" (2022) https://www.healthit.gov/playbook/\",\"World Wide Web Consortium, \\\"Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1\\\" (2021) https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/\",\"OWASP Foundation, \\\"OWASP Top 10 - 2021\\\" https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/\",\"Amazon Web Services, \\\"HIPAA Eligible Services\\\" (2023) https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/hipaa-compliance/\",\"Microsoft Azure, \\\"Azure for Healthcare and HIPAA\\\" (2023) https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/healthcare-apis/\",\"Google Cloud, \\\"Cloud Healthcare API\\\" (2023) https://cloud.google.com/healthcare-api\",\"ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Information security management standards (2022) https://www.iso.org/standard/75652.html\"]}"
